  "notes": "Authored for due2; no origin result. Closes the rest of the gap of #30. ex:viaManager applies in every scenario and waits on ex:managerApproval, so every completion is Pending. Each ex:viaDeskN applies only when its desk flag is true and demands ex:managerApproval and its own review, so ex:viaManager dominates it whenever it applies, and every completion's frontier is [[ex:managerApproval]]. The relevant unknowns of due2-workflows.md §6.4 are the variables of the uncertain candidates' U parts: one per unknown flag. With nine, more than max_frontier_vars (8), W3 does not enumerate them: it lists the routes of the candidates that are ready or pending whatever the unknowns are, and reports frontier_complete and exact false (decisions/0004 #4), although enumeration would give true. With eight, at the bound, it enumerates all 2^8 assignments and finds the frontier complete. A backend with no fallback (clingo-i, exact_only) is not asked scenario 1.",
